			{itemID=182144,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=186599,diffs={109},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=22844,title="Overview",body="Infused Goliaths defend the outer perimeter before The Tarragrue, offering potent Anima Powers when defeated.\n\nIn battle, The Tarragrue attempts to pick off defenseless targets with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:347269|h[Chains of Eternity]|h|r while gathering power. Upon reaching 100 energy, The Tarragrue dissolves into Torghast's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:347679|h[Hungering Mist]|h|r and stalks its prey with a series of crushing assaults.\n\nAt 10% health remaining, the Jailer removes Anima Powers from all players and sends The Tarragrue into a wild frenzy."},
			{id=22845,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;|cFF2959D3|Hspell:346986|h[Crushed Armor]|h|r stuns the current target and applies a large Physical damage vulnerability.\n$bullet;There is a gap in |cFF2959D3|Hspell:347671|h[Hungering Mist]|h|r that can be used to avoid damage."},
			{id=22846,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;|cFF2959D3|Hspell:347269|h[Chains of Eternity]|h|r stuns and then destroys the first player caught in a line.\n$bullet;There is a gap in |cFF2959D3|Hspell:347671|h[Hungering Mist]|h|r that can be used to avoid damage."},
			{id=22847,title="Healers",body="$bullet;Dispel players afflicted with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:347283|h[Predator's Howl]|h|r.\n$bullet;|cFF2959D3|Hspell:347269|h[Chains of Eternity]|h|r stuns and then destroys the first player caught in a line.\n$bullet;There is a gap in |cFF2959D3|Hspell:347671|h[Hungering Mist]|h|r that can be used to avoid damage."},
			{id=23609,title="Stage One: Confronting the Terror",difficultyIDs={14,15,16}},
			{id=23610,title="Chain Thing"},
			{id=23611,title="Section 16"},
			{id=23612,title="Hungering Mist"},
			{id=23734,title="Section 17",difficultyIDs={15}},
			{id=23735,title="Section 18"},
			{id=23736,title="Section 19"},
			{id=23737,title="Section 20"},
			{id=23613,title="Section 17",body="$[!16\n\nIn Mythic difficulty, the Jailer summons forth two forgotten Torments and their afflictions on players last until The Tarragrue is defeated.$]",difficultyIDs={16}},
